							<p class="MsoNormal" align="center"><font color="#ffffff"><i><b><font face="Georgia" size="6"><span style="COLOR: blue"></span></font></b></i><span style="COLOR: blue"></span></font></p> <p align="center"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font color="#ffffff" size="6"><em><strong><img src="/pics/1602/Newmembers.jpg" /></strong></em></font></p> <div class="MsoNormal" style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><font color="#ffffff"> <hr align="center" width="100%" size="2" /> </font></div></span> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font color="#ffffff" size="2">1. Read the guild charter and guild rules and make sure you understand them fully.</font></p> <p><font face="Verdana" size="2"><font color="#ffffff"><font face="Times New Roman">2. The notification of membership/denial will be made on boards&nbsp;and in e-mail</font>.</font></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font color="#ffffff" size="2">3. &nbsp;New members gain&nbsp;DKP just like established members. However, new members cannot vote on raid or guild bank items, until they have been with the guild for 30 days.&nbsp; (The exceptions to this rule are listed under the </font><a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1035"><font color="#ffffff" size="2">Rules and Regulations</font></a><font size="2"><font color="#ffffff">)<?xml:namespace prefix = o /><o:p></o:p></font></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font size="2"><font color="#ffffff">4. &nbsp;New members cannot become officers or raid looters during their 30-day probationary period. <o:p></o:p></font></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font color="#ffffff" size="2">5.&nbsp; If a person would like to join Moonlite Redemption, they can apply at the website by filling out the </font><a href="/application.aspx"><font color="#ffffff" size="2">application</font></a><font size="2"><font color="#ffffff">.&nbsp; Tell us a little about yourself such as your character name, class and level, as well as why you would like to join MR, etc.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></font></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font size="2"><font color="#ffffff">6.&nbsp; We take characters of all races and classes. The minimum level requirement is 55, excluding alts. <o:p></o:p></font></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font size="2"><font color="#ffffff">7.&nbsp; A full member must sponsor new members during their probationary period. The sponsor is responsible for reporting any misconduct, and making sure that new members understand the guild rules and regulations. <o:p></o:p></font></font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font color="#ffffff"><font size="2">8.&nbsp; Reports of misconduct may result in immediate removal. All probationary members are subject to removal with or without previous notification or reason.</font> </font></span></p> <p class="MsoNormal" align="center"><span style="COLOR: blue"><font color="#ffffff"><font size="5"><em><strong><font color="#0000ff">Membership Requirements Detailed:</font></strong></em><font size="3">&nbsp;</font></font><o:p></o:p></font></span></p><span style="COLOR: blue"> <div class="MsoNormal" style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align="center"><font color="#ffffff"> <hr align="center" width="100%" size="2" /> </font></div></span><span style="COLOR: blue"> <p><font color="#ffffff" size="2">Probationary period exists for all new members. There are essentially&nbsp;4 requirements to be met before you become a "Full Member". </font></p> <blockquote dir="ltr" style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px"> <p><font color="#ffffff" size="2">A. You must be level 55+.</font></p> <p><font size="2"><font color="#ffffff">B.&nbsp; You must fill out an </font><a href="/application.aspx"><font color="#ffffff">application</font></a><font color="#ffffff">.</font></font></p> <p><font color="#ffffff" size="2">C. You must be a member for 4 weeks depending on your level of dedication to the guild and its members at the time.</font></p> <p><font color="#ffffff" size="2">D. You must not violate any guild rules during this period, if you do so in bad standing, you jeopardize your membership.</font></p></blockquote> <p dir="ltr" align="right"><font color="#ffffff" size="2">*Almost no rule is all-inclusive.</font></span></p>
							
